had le Clos"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The final saw the early lead taken by Čavić and German " [:a {:href "/athletes/115646"} "Steffen Deibler"] ", with Phelps seventh at 50 metres, leading only Le Clos. But the final lap was all Phelps as he finished in 51.21 to three-peat in the event, with Le Clos also coming on strong to finish in a second-place tie with Russian " [:a {:href "/athletes/103902"} "Yevgeny Korotyshkin"] ". Fourth-place was also a dead-heat between Deibler and Čavić."] "\n\n" [:p {} "For Phelps this was his final individual gold medal of a vaunted Olympic career. It was his 11th individual gold medal and 17th gold medal in all – he would later win #18 in the 4×100 medley relay. His three-peat in this event followed a similar three-peat he had just completed in the 200 IM, making him the first man to three-peat in a swimming event at the Olympics, and only the third person ever, following Australian " [:a {:href "/athletes/45044"} "Dawn Fraser"] " in the 100 freestyle in 1956-64, and Hungarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/48094"} "Krisztina Egerszegi"] " in the 100 backstroke in 1988-96."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/93860"} "Michael Phelps"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "51.72 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "50.86 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "51.21 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/121715"} "Chad le Clos"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RSA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RSA.png"}] "RSA"]] [:td {} "